{"line":408,"clause":"L408","pdf_page":"9","status":"GAP","excerpt":"Let $W\\in\\R^2$ have a density bounded by $L$, and let $q$ be a quadratic polynomial on $\\R^2$ whose quadratic part has a definite symmetric matrix $B$. Then $q(W)$ has a density bounded by $\\pi L/\\sqrt{\\det B}$.","hypotheses":"As printed","derivation":"The quantitative definite pushforward estimate is correct after C01, but the literal proof uses the defective chart wording at line 412.","dependencies":"C01","downstream":"Final definite-pair branch inherits literal gap.","source_commit":"ec211ba2d77a4a9850168c6af1574ea651feaa7c","source_tex_blob":"c4f2a997cf336ee974e15409b5bccdd8cca039d8","source_pdf_sha256":"4c1a8eb808b32739625aa475c1aad24dc857a3f35fc960504b371487f2850423","account":"account03","slot":"B12","run_id":"20260925T014656Z-account03-B12-lineaudit-r68","pass_id":"P1-B12-forward-from-line1","pdf_render_note":"Page mapping follows package anchors; direct screenshot unavailable."}
